 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This Thursday, you left again\nThe light of your face and forehead;\nAnd now these shadows darken again.\nIt is enough for me to believe\nThat you are not dead in that darkness.\nBut what have you said? replied\nPoesy. You have been talking about me\nWho am none but poetry's boyne daughter.\nHe who speaks is speaking well or nothing.\nShe who smiles is smiling well or pretending\nTo be most lonely by divining there\nThe joy that lives in beauty.",
